1.7.m:
At the end of a thousand yugas, these [worlds] perish again and again;
then, O king, Brahmā and the others will indeed attain union with Viṣṇu.

Thus ends the seventh chapter, titled "Description of the Manvantaras," in the first book, the Sṛṣṭikhaṇḍa, of the glorious Padma Purāṇa.

1.8.m:
Pulastya said:
Vivasvat was born of old to Kaśyapa from Aditi;
he had three wives: Saṃjñā, Rājñī, and Prabhā.
